   "evidence": "`Set.prod` and `Set.Ioc` are both in Mathlib; `mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/Constructions/SumProd.lean:534 theorem interior_prod_eq (s : Set X) (t : Set Y) : interior (s \u00d7\u02e2 t) = interior s \u00d7\u02e2 interior t` and `:537 frontier_prod_eq` are the API made unavailable by the `setOf` spelling.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Kinematics/Domain.lean",
   "fix": "Define `elasticLine (S : \u211d) : Set (\u211d \u00d7 \u211d) := ({1} : Set \u211d) \u00d7\u02e2 Set.Ioc 0 S`. `mem_elasticLine` stays `Iff.rfl` (`Set.mem_prod` unfolds to `z.1 \u2208 {1} \u2227 z.2 \u2208 Ioc 0 S`, i.e. `z.1 = 1 \u2227 0 < z.2 \u2227 z.2 \u2264 S`), so `kinematicDomain_inter_fst_eq_one`, `elasticLine_subset_kinematicDomain` and `elasticLine_subset_frontier` are unaffected.",
   "issue": "`elasticLine S := {z | z.1 = 1 \u2227 0 < z.2 \u2227 z.2 \u2264 S}` spells out a set that is exactly the Mathlib product `({1} : Set \u211d) \u00d7\u02e2 Set.Ioc 0 S`, so it is cut off from the whole `Set.prod` / product-measure API (`interior_prod_eq`, `frontier_prod_eq`, `measure_prod_prod`) that the announced \u00a71.4 tail-support work on this line will want.",
   "line": "82"
  }
